<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link><description>India News Today: Get latest India news and breaking news from India on Times of India. TOI brings the top news headlines from India on Politics, Elections, Current Affairs and more</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-05T04:55:19+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/-2128936835.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Mon, 05 Oct 2026 04:55:19 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Democracy in peril as voters illegally ousted: Former SC judge Justice Rohinton Fali Nariman]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/democracy-in-peril-as-voters-illegally-ousted-former-sc-judge-justice-rohinton-fali-nariman/articleshow/134680618.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134680618.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Justice Rohinton Fali Nariman expressed concerns regarding the functioning of the Election Commission in India. He highlighted the issue of illegal removal of voters from electoral lists, especially in West Bengal. Nariman noted that 90 lakh voters were disenfranchised, with many not having access to justice. He emphasized the need for reform in the appointment process of election commissioners to ensure fairness.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/democracy-in-peril-as-voters-illegally-ousted-former-sc-judge-justice-rohinton-fali-nariman/articleshow/134680618.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/democracy-in-peril-as-voters-illegally-ousted-former-sc-judge-justice-rohinton-fali-nariman/articleshow/134680618.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-05T03:34:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Amit Anand Choudhary</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134680631,imgsize-52346.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[1 dead as Russian drones hit desi pharma plant in Ukraine]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/1-dead-as-russian-drones-hit-desi-pharma-plant-in-ukraine/articleshow/134680367.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134680367.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In Ukraine's Sumy region, six Russian drones attacked the Kusum Group's pharmaceutical plant, killing one engineer and injuring others. The main structure of the facility was largely destroyed during the targeted strike, which occurs amid a pattern of similar attacks. The company estimates damage from this incident could exceed $50 million, impacting operations significantly.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/1-dead-as-russian-drones-hit-desi-pharma-plant-in-ukraine/articleshow/134680367.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/1-dead-as-russian-drones-hit-desi-pharma-plant-in-ukraine/articleshow/134680367.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-05T02:40:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Anuja Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134680382,imgsize-108296.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[External affairs minister S Jaishankar says US has chosen to become 'lonelier power']]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/external-affairs-minister-s-jaishankar-says-us-has-chosen-to-become-lonelier-power/articleshow/134680336.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134680336.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[S Jaishankar stated that India aims to mediate in the Russia-Ukraine conflict through dialogue and diplomacy. India has recently proposed ideas addressing issues like grain and energy exports to both nations. Jaishankar emphasized America's changing global position and the implications of China's rise on international relations. India is also facing domestic repercussions due to the ongoing conflict, including commercial shipping disruptions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/external-affairs-minister-s-jaishankar-says-us-has-chosen-to-become-lonelier-power/articleshow/134680336.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/external-affairs-minister-s-jaishankar-says-us-has-chosen-to-become-lonelier-power/articleshow/134680336.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-05T02:29:51+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sachin Parashar</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134680356,imgsize-50000.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[25 paisa/kg wheat MSP hike an 'insult': Samyukta Kisan Morcha]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/25p/kg-wheat-msp-hike-an-insult-samyukta-kisan-morcha/articleshow/134680324.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134680324.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Farmer organisations represented by Samyukta Kisan Morcha rejected the government's announced minimum support prices for Rabi crops. They described the small increase for wheat as an insult rather than acceptable compensation. SKM called for a revision of MSPs and urged states to offer bonuses to farmers. Additionally, they highlighted the impact of rising diesel and input costs on farming.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/25p/kg-wheat-msp-hike-an-insult-samyukta-kisan-morcha/articleshow/134680324.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/25p/kg-wheat-msp-hike-an-insult-samyukta-kisan-morcha/articleshow/134680324.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-05T02:22:01+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134680326,imgsize-360958.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Look Out Circular' against parents of man who secretly took away child to US]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/look-out-circular-against-parents-of-man-who-secretly-took-away-child-to-us/articleshow/134680302.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134680302.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Supreme Court has indicated consequences for parents of a man who abducted his daughter to the US. This decision came during a case regarding child custody between NRI couples. The father has been ordered to return to India with the child within four weeks. If he fails to comply, his parents will face legal consequences. The court emphasizes the importance of the child's connection with her mother.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/look-out-circular-against-parents-of-man-who-secretly-took-away-child-to-us/articleshow/134680302.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/look-out-circular-against-parents-of-man-who-secretly-took-away-child-to-us/articleshow/134680302.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-05T02:13:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Amit Anand Choudhary</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134680312,imgsize-153452.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[SIR strikes at heart of Constitution: Supreme Court judge Justice Ujjal Bhuyan]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sir-strikes-at-heart-of-constitution-supreme-court-judge-justice-ujjal-bhuyan/articleshow/134680179.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134680179.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Justice Ujjal Bhuyan condemned the extensive deletion of voter names from electoral rolls due to the special intensive revision process. He emphasized that such actions undermine the core principles of the Indian Constitution and disenfranchise millions of citizens. Bhuyan highlighted that the right to vote is essential for free and fair elections in India. He urged that no citizen should be denied the right to vote without due process.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sir-strikes-at-heart-of-constitution-supreme-court-judge-justice-ujjal-bhuyan/articleshow/134680179.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sir-strikes-at-heart-of-constitution-supreme-court-judge-justice-ujjal-bhuyan/articleshow/134680179.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-05T01:34:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dhananjay Mahapatra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134680197,imgsize-85376.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Jammu and Kashmir: Pakistani prisoner dies by suicide in  jail]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jammu-and-kashmir-pakistani-prisoner-dies-by-suicide-in-jail/articleshow/134679864.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134679864.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Shahid Imran, a 36-year-old Pakistani undertrial prisoner, was found unconscious in his jail cell early Sunday. He was a resident of Sargooda district in Punjab, Pakistan. Authorities rushed him to GMCH where doctors declared him brought dead. The incident occurred at the high-security central jail in Jammu. An investigation into the circumstances surrounding his death is likely to follow.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jammu-and-kashmir-pakistani-prisoner-dies-by-suicide-in-jail/articleshow/134679864.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jammu-and-kashmir-pakistani-prisoner-dies-by-suicide-in-jail/articleshow/134679864.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-05T00:37:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sanjay Khajuria</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134679933,imgsize-900842.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kashmiri teacher fights period stigma, one village at a time]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kashmiri-teacher-fights-period-stigma-one-village-at-a-time/articleshow/134679820.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134679820.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Aasima Jan works diligently in north Kashmir, focusing on menstrual health awareness to help girls stay in school. She began her efforts after witnessing the stigma around menstruation affecting attendance rates among female students. Monthly sessions in villages educate families about menstrual hygiene and encourage open discussion about the topic. Aasima also distributes sanitary pads, highlighting their importance for health and hygiene.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kashmiri-teacher-fights-period-stigma-one-village-at-a-time/articleshow/134679820.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kashmiri-teacher-fights-period-stigma-one-village-at-a-time/articleshow/134679820.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-05T00:33:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Naseer Ganai</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134679857,imgsize-89105.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Beyond advocacy: Government steps up diplomatic push for Ukraine settlement]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/beyond-advocacy-government-steps-up-diplomatic-push-for-ukraine-settlement/articleshow/134678878.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134678878.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/beyond-advocacy-government-steps-up-diplomatic-push-for-ukraine-settlement/articleshow/134678878.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/beyond-advocacy-government-steps-up-diplomatic-push-for-ukraine-settlement/articleshow/134678878.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T23:17:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sachin Parashar</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134678889,imgsize-53986.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Little bit more involved': Jaishankar says India has 'gone beyond advocacy' to end Russia-Ukraine war]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/little-bit-more-involved-jaishankar-says-india-has-gone-beyond-advocacy-to-end-russia-ukraine-war/articleshow/134678353.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134678353.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/little-bit-more-involved-jaishankar-says-india-has-gone-beyond-advocacy-to-end-russia-ukraine-war/articleshow/134678353.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/little-bit-more-involved-jaishankar-says-india-has-gone-beyond-advocacy-to-end-russia-ukraine-war/articleshow/134678353.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T22:39:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134678358,imgsize-144226.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Singeetham Srinivasa Rao: Seven decades, many worlds of cinema]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/singeetham-srinivasa-rao-seven-decades-many-worlds-of-cinema/articleshow/134678197.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134678197.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/singeetham-srinivasa-rao-seven-decades-many-worlds-of-cinema/articleshow/134678197.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/singeetham-srinivasa-rao-seven-decades-many-worlds-of-cinema/articleshow/134678197.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T22:36:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Chethan Kumar</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134678222,imgsize-197564.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Mumbai Police registers FIR against organisers of Thackerays' anti-SIR march]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/mumbai-police-registers-fir-against-organisers-of-thackerays-anti-sir-march/articleshow/134677950.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134677950.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/mumbai-police-registers-fir-against-organisers-of-thackerays-anti-sir-march/articleshow/134677950.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/mumbai-police-registers-fir-against-organisers-of-thackerays-anti-sir-march/articleshow/134677950.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-04T21:59:27+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134677990,imgsize-236118.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[India successfully demonstrates its first free-space quantum-secure communication link for over 5.5 km]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-successfully-demonstrates-its-first-free-space-quantum-secure-communication-link-for-over-5-5-km/articleshow/134677875.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134677875.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In a groundbreaking trial, Indian startup QNu Labs, in collaboration with BISAG-N and IIT Gandhinagar, successfully tested free-space quantum key distribution. This trial established a secure quantum communication channel over a considerable distance, boasting a quantum bit error rate of under 5%. With the integration into BISAG-N’s Vedic Kavach platform, secure key sharing and end-to-end message encryption are now possible, paving the way for advancements in India’s secure communication framework.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-successfully-demonstrates-its-first-free-space-quantum-secure-communication-link-for-over-5-5-km/articleshow/134677875.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-success